Single-database configuration for Flask-Migrate.

Typical workflow:
1) flask --app catanatron_server:create_app db upgrade -d catanatron_server/migrations
2) flask --app catanatron_server:create_app db migrate -d catanatron_server/migrations -m "describe change"
3) flask --app catanatron_server:create_app db upgrade -d catanatron_server/migrations

If the database already contains tables created by old `db.create_all()` startup behavior:
1) flask --app catanatron_server:create_app db stamp -d catanatron_server/migrations 20260513_01
2) Continue with normal migrate/upgrade flow for later revisions.
